  "name": "Example: Determining Whether a Function is Left- or Right-Continuous From a Graph",
  "problem": "Is the function $y=g(x)$ below left-continuous at $x=0?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945035/assets/03166feaa94b64b4fbdfac1096b0e0d771abf5b4a47e84a6e28dbed257540c6b.png)",
  "worked_solution": "To determine whether $g(x),$ is left-continuous at $x=0,$ we need to check whether the left-sided limit is equal to the function value.\n\nIndeed, we see that\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to 0^-} g(x) = -2 = g(0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=0.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
